# Wave W17-AC (Route 230): palm rock — harbour-point rock: a warm brown boulder standing at the harbour point, foam collar at its base, the last stone of the circuit (design: north at the point — Clashfield harbour; the point’s rocks take the harbour’s weather). The baked water is the shipped sea entire — the register is carried by the boulder’s warm face, never by a mismatched water square. Route 230’s own rock — split from its twin Route 229’s headland rock by face entire (warm harbour brown vs grey-green headland) and from Route 219’s jetty rock by office: this stone closes a circuit, that one opens a lane.
